<title>FRANCE: EU trade shows 568,000 T wheat deals for Africa.</title>
<headline>EU trade shows 568,000 T wheat deals for Africa.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-12-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Grain traders have presented contracts to the European Commission to export a total of 568,000 tonnes of wheat to Africa under a special European Union refund scheme, member-country officials said.</p>
<p>EU grain officials initially put the tally at around 550,000 tonnes.</p>
<p>But final data submitted by member countries indicated that in France traders showed contracts to export 528,000 tonnes of wheat.</p>
<p>In the Netherlands they presented deals to ship 40,000 tonnes of wheat.  </p>
<p>By proving sale of the wheat, traders will qualify for long-term export licences at a refund of 28 Ecus per tonne as part of an EU plan to offer preferential terms to a group of hard-pressed African countries.</p>
<p>The deadline for showing the contracts was 1500 GMT on Wednesday.</p>
<p>-- Paris newsroom +331 4221 5432</p>
